; ============================================================================
; cp_map.ini.example - STARTING POINT for a fresh Channel Points deployment
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Copy to cp_map.ini (same folder) and edit freely.  This example ships
; EMPTY-BY-DEFAULT (all rows commented): rewards with no entry are logged and
; ignored by cp_listen.py - the safe default.  (The repo's cp_map.ini holds
; lane's own reward catalog; that is content, not a hardcode.)
;
; Matching is CASE-INSENSITIVE and whitespace-collapsed.  The game
; re-validates every verb and its own gates, so a wrong mapping can never
; crash anything - it just gets dropped with a RESULT line.
;
; ROW GRAMMAR (uncomment and adapt):
;   my reward name = flip            -> verb (game default duration)
;   spawn a bird = spawn raven 2     -> verb + arg words
;   long effect = confuse @600       -> explicit duration, FRAMES (60 = 1 s)
;   say it = hurt {input}            -> {input} = redeemer's typed message
;                                       (sanitized: '|' and control chars
;                                       stripped, capped at 40 chars)
;   broken reward = -                -> explicitly disabled, stays visible
;
; Valid verbs mirror src/twitch.c kVerbs[] (heal hurt mp drain refill rupees
; tax bombs arrows smite clearscreen spawn swarm confuse flip party freeze
; stun curse root steal rob thief pickpocket speed fast slow ice icefloor
; illusion bunny fairy deny arise chicken cucco).  "World" verbs (smite,
; spawn, arise, ...) only fire while Link is in actual gameplay; vs_mode=1
; blocks the "helpful" ones (heal, mp, refill, ...).
; ============================================================================
[map]

; --- sample rows: uncomment to try -------------------------------------------
;arise chicken!! (athf) = arise
;flashbang the stream = flip
;duck vanishes = spawn raven 2
